Honestly, if your budget is tight, the Hybride is the smarter buy. It already gives you the core benefits: pocket springs, 7 comfort layers, stable support, and a semi-firm feel. You are not settling for a basic mattress.

The Hybride Premium is worth the extra only if you specifically want:

a more cushioned, balanced feel;
2 additional centimetres and one extra comfort layer;
thicker foam for more precise support;
a reversible comfort layer, with a softer or firmer side;
better movement absorption if you sleep with a partner.

So my honest recommendation for you is: choose the Hybride. Choose the Premium only if one of those comfort features is important enough to justify the additional cost. Both are designed as substantial hybrid mattresses, but the Premium is an upgrade in comfort and adjustability, not a completely different level of product.

